      "widgets_values": [
        "Flux.2 text-to-image with the Y7 Flux.2 Sampler\n\nThe plainest possible Flux.2 setup: an empty latent, a prompt, and one\nsampler node that does the rest. Nothing else is wired.\n\nPress Run. To get a different picture, change the seed on the sampler\n(it is set to randomize, so every run already gives you a new one).\n\nRepoint the three loaders at your own files before running.\n\nThis example is set up for a distilled Flux.2 Klein checkpoint:\n\n  diffusion model - flux-2-klein-9b.safetensors\n  text encoder    - qwen_3_8b.safetensors  (type: flux2)\n  vae             - flux2-klein-vae.safetensors\n\nIf you run a NON-distilled Flux.2 model instead, raise `steps` on the\nsampler (20-30 is normal) and set `cfg` to something above 1.0."
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
    {
      "id": 41,
      "type": "Note",
      "pos": [
        360,
        460
      ],
      "size": [
        400,
        480
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 10,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {
        "cnr_id": "comfy-core",
        "Node name for S&R": "Note"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "Y7 Flux.2 Sampler\n\nThis one node replaces the five you would normally wire up for Flux.2:\nRandomNoise, KSamplerSelect, Flux2Scheduler, CFGGuider and\nSamplerCustomAdvanced. Give it a model, a latent and your two\nconditionings, and it hands back the finished latent to decode.\n\nThere is no width/height here on purpose. The schedule Flux.2 needs\ndepends on the picture size, and the node reads that straight off the\nlatent coming in, so the two can never disagree.\n\n  seed        - change it for a different picture\n  cfg         - leave at 1.0 for distilled Klein checkpoints. They are\n                trained so the negative prompt is ignored anyway\n  sampler_name- euler is the safe default\n  steps       - 4 is enough for distilled Klein. A full Flux.2 model\n                wants far more\n  denoise     - leave at 1.0. On Flux.2 this is NOT an image-to-image\n                strength dial; see the node's docs for why"
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
    {
      "id": 42,
      "type": "Note",
      "pos": [
        -140,
        640
      ],
      "size": [
        420,
        240
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 11,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {
        "cnr_id": "comfy-core",
        "Node name for S&R": "Note"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "Size of the picture\n\nEmpty Flux 2 Latent sets how big the finished picture is. Width and\nheight must divide by 16. Flux.2 is built for around one megapixel, so\n1024 x 1024 (square), 1152 x 896 (landscape) or 896 x 1152 (portrait)\nare all good starting points. Much bigger and quality usually drops.\n\nThe negative prompt goes through ConditioningZeroOut because Klein is\nguidance-distilled and runs at cfg 1.0, where the negative is ignored\nanyway. If you raise cfg above 1.0, swap this for a real prompt."
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    }
